// src/v4/std/text.dag
//
// Scope: Unicode text — code points (`Char`) and strings (`String`).
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode
//         (Char = a Unicode scalar value / code point)
//
// Owns:
//   - Char — a Unicode scalar value carrier, delivered as unrefined `Nat`
//     with the code-point-range / surrogate-exclusion refinement tracked as
//     a bounded scaffold below
//   - String — `FreeMonoid<Char>`
//   - inhabitance: String inhabits `FreeMonoid<Char>` (std/algebra.dag) —
//     concatenation / empty fall out of the free monoid
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/nat.dag: Nat (a code point is a bounded Nat)
//   - std/algebra.dag: FreeMonoid
//   (The original scaffold's `std/node.dag: Cardinality` entry is
//   superseded by the header reconcile below: text.dag does not consume
//   node.dag's Cardinality connective today.)
//
// Status: T-3 modeled 2026-05-16 (wise-dove-896). Replaces part of the
//   deleted std/primitive.dag; see src/v4/STRUCTURE.md §"scalar/numeric
//   concept decomposition".
//
// HEADER RECONCILE (worker-tier Extent-🟡 value-refinement class,
// 2026-05-16). The frozen scaffold header named `Char` as a
// `Cardinality`-bounded `Nat` excluding surrogates and listed
// `std/node.dag: Cardinality` as a consumed dependency. The delivered
// carrier is intentionally `type Char = Nat`: v2 syntax plus this file's
// settled deps (`nat` + `algebra`) cannot express the Unicode scalar set
// U+0000..U+D7FF ∪ U+E000..U+10FFFF as a type-enforced value refinement,
// and a single upper-bound interval would admit surrogate code points
// (fabricated Char). This follows the diagnostic.dag `Extent.ByteRange`
// 🟡 precedent: keep the honest carrier, document the illegal states the
// current substrate cannot exclude, bound producer use, and name the
// dissolution trigger. It also follows the operator-ratified
// collection.dag b2 header reconcile pattern: when a frozen Cardinality
// wording names an unbuildable refinement, reconcile the header to the
// actual carrier and mark the refinement deferred-out rather than
// pretending to consume node.dag's Cardinality connective. The `Owns`,
// `Consumes`, and `Status` lines above reflect this reconcile; the
// `String = FreeMonoid<Char>` alias edge remains the machine-readable
// inhabitance authority.


module v4.std.text


import v4.std.algebra { FreeMonoid, free_monoid_is_empty }
import v4.std.nat { Nat }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// STRING INHABITANCE IS MACHINE-READABLE. `String` is a type alias onto
// `FreeMonoid<Char>` below. That alias edge is the inhabitance edge: a
// consumer does not read prose or a side table to learn that strings are
// finite character sequences. This is the same authority pattern as
// collection.dag's `List<T> = FreeMonoid<T>`.
//
// CHAR RANGE IS A TRACKED SCAFFOLD. Unicode scalar values are exactly
// U+0000..U+D7FF and U+E000..U+10FFFF: natural-number code points in
// the Unicode codespace, excluding surrogate code points. The current
// v2 syntax and this file's settled dependency set (`nat` + `algebra`)
// cannot express that non-contiguous bounded subset as a
// type-enforced value refinement. A single upper-bound interval would
// admit surrogates, which would be a fabricated `Char`.
//
// The honest T-3 carrier is therefore the unrefined `Nat` alias below,
// with these bridge properties:
//   (a) scaffold doc — THIS note; `Char` currently names the code-point
//       carrier but does not type-enforce the Unicode scalar subset.
//   (b) bounds on use — producers of `Char` must construct only Unicode
//       scalar values. A surrogate-valued `Char` is a producer bug
//       against this scaffold, not a legal Unicode scalar value.
//   (c) dissolution trigger — when v4 has a machine-readable value
//       refinement for finite unions of ordered `Nat` intervals (or an
//       equivalent Unicode-scalar predicate substrate) in the settled
//       dependency path, replace this alias with the refined carrier:
//       U+0000..U+D7FF ∪ U+E000..U+10FFFF.
//
// No coproduct is introduced in this file. `String` aliases the
// `FreeMonoid<T>` construction owned by std/algebra.dag, whose own
// Practice-4 ledger lives there; `Char` is an alias over `Nat`, whose
// ledger lives in std/nat.dag. This file therefore has no new
// Practice-4 ledger.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Char — Unicode scalar value carrier.
//
// Terminal target: a bounded `Nat` over Unicode scalar values
// (U+0000..U+D7FF and U+E000..U+10FFFF). Current v2-expressible shape:
// an unrefined `Nat` alias with the tracked scaffold above. This keeps
// the code-point parent faithful while avoiding the false single-range
// model that would admit surrogate code points.
type Char = Nat


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// String — finite sequence of `Char`.
//
// The alias IS the machine-readable inhabitance edge:
// `String` inhabits `FreeMonoid<Char>` by being the free-monoid carrier
// over `Char`. Concatenation, empty, fold, and length are structural
// reads of std/algebra.dag's `FreeMonoid<T>` shape, not operations
// re-declared in this file.
type String = FreeMonoid<Char>


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// string_is_empty — canonical **boundary query** for `String`.
//
// `String` is `FreeMonoid<Char>` (alias edge above). Emptiness is
// std/algebra.dag's `free_monoid_is_empty` on that carrier — not a
// per-consumer spine walk.
fn string_is_empty(s: String) -> Bool {
  free_monoid_is_empty(xs: s)
}
